 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** $O(1)$. Fixed number of arithmetic operations for $3 \times 3$ transpose and $3 \times 1$ matrix-vector multiplication.
-*   **Memory Complexity:** $O(1)$. Requires storage for one $4 \times 4$ matrix or one quaternion and one vector.
-*   **Strengths:** Avoids expensive $4 \times 4$ matrix inversion; numerically stable for orthogonal rotations.
-*   **Limitations:** Assumes valid SE3 input (orthogonal rotation matrix or unit quaternion); does not handle scaling or shearing.
-*   **Measured Performance:** Not given in the sources.
-*   **When to use:** Converting coordinates between camera/world and local/object frames in ray generation or rasterization pipelines.
